<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Wright (governor)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1716">1716</a>–<a href="/years/1785">1785</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Sir James Wright, 1st Baronet</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James Wright was the last royal governor of the Province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>, serving from 1760. Under him <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> plantations worked by enslaved Africans spread along the coast, and Georgia's frontier was extended by land cessions from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscogee">Creek</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cherokee">Cherokee</a>. Patriots drove him out in 1776, but he returned in 1779 after British forces reoccupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savannah">Savannah</a> and governed there until the British evacuation in 1782.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-wright-governor.jpg" alt="James Wright (governor)" width="320" height="428" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andrea Soldi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:James_Wright_(governor).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
